  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "During Apollo 11, the 1969 mission that first landed people on the Moon, the crew is said to have looked at Aristarchus, a crater on the Moon, after astronomers in Germany reported it looked unusually bright. A researcher on the show tells it second-hand, naming the crew, Neil Armstrong, Buzz Aldrin and Michael Collins, and offering only that \"apparently\" the German astronomers had seen the glow. It belongs to a group of stories claiming the Apollo 11 astronauts saw strange things on or near the Moon."
